## Scenario

The research copilot answers an engineering question: which local engine should power Tuff's screenshot OCR. It shows its process first (search, read, benchmark a sample set, weigh the trade-offs), then gives a conclusion with numbered citations, a comparison table, pageable insights and a recommendation card. Clicking a citation in the conclusion switches the evidence rail on the right to the matching source or retrieved chunk and highlights it.

It fits answer engines, knowledge-base Q&A, technology selection and competitive research: anywhere a conclusion has to be traceable. Accuracy, speed and size claims about third-party engines in this template are qualitative or sample data, not measurements.

