## Anatomy

| Region | Components | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Header | [TxWorkingIndicator](/docs/dev/components/working-indicator), [TxStatusBadge](/docs/dev/components/status-badge) | The current research phase and its elapsed time, the done state |
| Research process | [TxChainOfThought](/docs/dev/components/chain-of-thought) | Search, read, benchmark, weigh: four steps unfold in turn and fold away once all of them settle |
| Conclusion | [TxInlineCitation](/docs/dev/components/inline-citation) | A plain paragraph revealed word by word, numbered citations popping in as they are reached; clicking one drives the rail |
| Comparison | [TxStreamMarkdown](/docs/dev/components/stream-markdown) | The comparison table and key points, streamed, with no links |
| Insights and recommendation | [TxInsightCards](/docs/dev/components/insight-cards), [TxRecommendationCard](/docs/dev/components/recommendation-card) | Three pageable insights (Chinese accuracy, first frame, size); the recommended plan and its alternatives, saved to notes once adopted |
| Follow-ups | [TxSuggestionChips](/docs/dev/components/suggestion-chips), [TxAiConversation](/docs/dev/components/ai-elements), [TxReasoningDisclosure](/docs/dev/components/reasoning-disclosure), [TxTypingIndicator](/docs/dev/components/typing-indicator) | Suggested follow-ups; a Q&A thread whose answers carry an expandable reasoning note |
| Evidence rail | [TxTabs](/docs/dev/components/tabs), [TxSources](/docs/dev/components/sources), [TxContextCards](/docs/dev/components/context-cards), [TxSignalMeter](/docs/dev/components/signal-meter), [TxSkeleton](/docs/dev/components/skeleton) | Sources / Chunks / Notes tabs; skeletons until the sources arrive; chunks rated for relevance |
| Notes | [TxMarkdownView](/docs/dev/components/markdown-view), [TxMessageActions](/docs/dev/components/message-actions) | The plan draft written once a recommendation is adopted, with copy |
| Input | [TxPromptBar](/docs/dev/components/prompt-bar) | Follow-up input; `@` to cite sources, `/` for commands, a research-mode picker |

## Interactions

- Research starts once the template scrolls into view and takes about 10 seconds: the research process, the conclusion word by word, the streamed comparison table, then insights, the recommendation and follow-ups. The window's Reset button or Research again in the header replays it.
- Click a numbered citation in the conclusion and the rail switches to the matching tab, scrolls only inside itself and rings the entry: citations with a retrieved chunk land on the chunk, the rest on the source. Clicking a source or a chunk's origin only shows "The host would open …" above the input; the page never navigates.
- The insight cards page through; the recommendation card opens its alternatives, and Save plan writes the draft into the Notes tab.
- A follow-up, or the follow-up pill inside an insight card, appends a question and a streamed answer with an expandable reasoning note; anything typed into the input gets a canned answer.
- While an answer streams, the answer column follows to the bottom; scroll up and it stops following, and the page itself never moves. In the docs column (640–959px) the rail uses tabs, from 960px it widens, and from 1200px the insights get a column of their own. Narrow (< 640px) hides the rail and puts the sources as stacked icons under the conclusion. With reduced motion the finished answer renders at once and reading starts from the top.

## Adapting it

- Wire a real service by mapping research steps onto TxChainOfThought's `steps` (keep exactly one `active` at a time), appending the conclusion token by token, and handing block content such as tables to TxStreamMarkdown.
- Clickable citations cannot live inside markdown: TxStreamMarkdown renders through `v-html`, which cannot hold components. Render the cited paragraph on its own, and keep links out of the markdown too, or they navigate the host.
- Scroll the evidence rail with its scroller's `scrollTo`, never `scrollIntoView`, which drags the whole page along.
- For claims about third-party products, write qualitative conclusions or label the numbers as sample data unless you measured them; give the recommendation's confidence a text label and use colour only to support it.
